              "path": "repairs[1].value",
              "before": "Strongest feature: Licona connects an early Pauline appearance tradition, disciples’ costly perseverance, Paul’s persecutor-to-adherent reversal, and James’s unbelief-to-leadership trajectory, establishing sincere conviction through convergent evidence. Principal limitation: Licona expressly concedes at events 190–192 that suffering supports sincerity, not truth; Carrier later accepts sincerity at 571–572 while proposing grief, suggestion, memory contamination, and distinct guilt-and-stress mechanisms at 585–619. Live burden: The contest is whether Licona’s later group-hallucination objection and challenge to evidence for Paul’s guilt at events 505–510 and 689–700 defeat Carrier’s mechanisms and bridge conviction to resurrection. Locked score: The fixed score of 86 rewards early, multiple, adverse-witness evidence and careful calibration, while recognizing that the move’s broader force depends on the later comparative-explanation dispute.",
              "after": "Strongest feature: Licona connects an early Pauline appearance tradition, disciples’ costly perseverance, Paul’s persecutor-to-adherent reversal, and James’s unbelief-to-leadership trajectory, establishing sincere conviction through convergent evidence. Principal limitation: Licona expressly concedes at 18:55–19:11 that suffering supports sincerity, not truth; Carrier later accepts sincerity at 55:23–55:32 while proposing grief, suggestion, memory contamination, and distinct guilt-and-stress mechanisms at 56:38–59:42. Live burden: The contest is whether Licona’s later group-hallucination objection and challenge to evidence for Paul’s guilt at 48:50–49:21 and 1:06:28–1:07:37 defeat Carrier’s mechanisms and bridge conviction to resurrection. Locked score: The fixed score of 86 rewards early, multiple, adverse-witness evidence and careful calibration, while recognizing that the move’s broader force depends on the later comparative-explanation dispute."
